### Notification API – endpoint smoke tests
### Open in VS Code (REST Client extension) or IntelliJ HTTP Client and click "Send Request".
### Server runs on port 8084 (see application.properties).

@host = http://localhost:8084
@base = {{host}}/api/notifications

### 1. createNotification -> 201 Created
# @name create
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "message": "Your account has been created.",
  "category": "CONTENT"
}

### 2. getAllNotifications -> 200 OK
GET {{base}}

### 3. getUnreadNotifications -> 200 OK (returns only status = UNREAD)
GET {{base}}/unread

### 4. updateNotification -> 200 OK (here we mark it as READ)
PUT {{base}}/{{create.response.body.notificationId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "message": "Your account has been created.",
  "category": "CONTENT",
  "status": "READ"
}

### 5. Confirm it no longer appears in unread -> 200 OK, empty list
GET {{base}}/unread
